# Adding an entity

The workflow for new entities and the follow-up code built on top of them.
Following this workflow keeps generated code uniform and lets agents produce
better additions.

## 1. Write the descriptor

Create `entities/Product.yaml` (PascalCase singular file name):

```yaml
name: Product
fields:
  - name: name
    type: String
    required: true
    minLength: 2
    maxLength: 100
  - name: price
    type: BigDecimal
    required: true
  - name: active
    type: boolean
    default: true

relations:
  - type: ManyToOne
    target: Category
    field: category
    required: true
```

Field types map to Java and TypeScript automatically; see the entity
descriptor documentation for the full list.

## 2. Generate

```bash
cleanstack entity Product          # from the workspace root
cleanstack regenerate entity Product   # after changing the descriptor
```

The command generates every artifact listed in
[naming-conventions.md](naming-conventions.md): JPA entity, repository,
service, controller, DTOs, mapper, exception, migration{{#if project.options.frontend}}, and the Angular
model, service, and list/detail/form pages{{/if}}.

## 3. Where agents add follow-up code

| Need | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Extra business rules for the entity | `cleanstack:user-code` region in `<Entity>Service` |
| Extra endpoints | New controller methods inside the region in `<Entity>Controller`, or a new controller class |
| Extra columns/fields | Update `entities/Product.yaml`, then `cleanstack regenerate entity Product` |
| Extra queries | Region in `<Entity>Repository` or a derived `@Query` method |
| Custom validation beyond the descriptor | Region in `<Entity>Request` or the mapper |
| New pages or components | New files under `src/app/pages/<route>/` following the naming contract |
| Cross-entity use cases | New service class in `service/`, named for the use case |

## 4. Verify

1. `cleanstack regenerate --dry-run` shows what changed before applying.
2. Backend: {{#if (eq project.options.buildTool "maven")}}`mvn clean verify`{{else}}`gradle clean build`{{/if}} in `{{kebabCase project.name}}-backend`.
{{#if project.options.frontend}}3. Frontend: `npm test` and `npm start` in `{{kebabCase project.name}}-ui`.
{{/if}}

## Do not

- Do not hand-write entity classes, repositories, controllers, DTOs, mappers,
  or CRUD pages; the generator owns them.
- Do not edit generated migrations to change a table; add a field to the
  descriptor and regenerate, which produces an update migration.
- Do not place custom code outside protected regions in generated files; see
  [protected-regions.md](protected-regions.md).

